<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S1" title="1 Introduction ‣ Lightweight Mixture of Experts for Efficient Multimodal Multi-task Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="69.18" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 69.18" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,69.18) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0.42 L 0 68.77 C 0 69 0.19 69.18 0.42 69.18 L 476.96 69.18 C 477.19 69.18 477.38 69 477.38 68.77 L 477.38 0.42 C 477.38 0.19 477.19 0 476.96 0 L 0.42 0 C 0.19 0 0 0.19 0 0.42 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#EDF8E8;" fill="#EDF8E8" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.42 0.42 L 0.42 68.77 L 476.96 68.77 L 476.96 0.42 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 5.95 56.8)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.62em;--ltx-fo-depth:3.83em;font-size:10pt;" height="61.44" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.51)" width="503.26"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.37em;">
<span id="A1.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Intuition:<span id="A1.p1.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Adding more experts refines the input space partitioning. Since the coarser partition’s output can be recovered from the finer partition (via a deterministic function), the finer partition cannot lose information about the label <math id="A1.p1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="A1.p1.pic1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(More experts cannot reduce label information under refinement)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X:\Omega\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X:\Omega\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y:\Omega\to\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y:\Omega\to\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> discrete and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(Y)&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(Y)&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
Fix <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{n-1}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\{1,\dots,n-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{n-1}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\{1,\dots,n-1\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{n}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\{1,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{n}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\{1,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math> be measurable routers, and let</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{n-1}:=r_{n-1}(X),\qquad Z_{n-1}:=A^{(n-1)}_{I_{n-1}}X," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{n-1}:=r_{n-1}(X),\qquad Z_{n-1}:=A^{(n-1)}_{I_{n-1}}X,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{n}:=r_{n}(X),\qquad Z_{n}:=A^{(n)}_{I_{n}}X," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{n}:=r_{n}(X),\qquad Z_{n}:=A^{(n)}_{I_{n}}X,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(n-1)}_{j},A^{(n)}_{e}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(n-1)}_{j},A^{(n)}_{e}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> are fixed linear maps.
Assume:</span></p>
<ol id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Factorization-on-support) For each </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\in\{1,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\in\{1,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> there exists </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{e}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{e}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that for all </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathsf{Supp}(X\mid I_{n}=e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝖲𝗎𝗉𝗉</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathsf{Supp}(X\mid I_{n}=e)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(n-1)}_{r_{n-1}(x)}x=R_{e}\,A^{(n)}_{e}x." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(n-1)}_{r_{n-1}(x)}x=R_{e}\,A^{(n)}_{e}x.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Identifiability) There exists measurable </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{e}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\{1,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{e}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\{1,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{n}=\hat{e}(Z_{n})\quad\text{a.s.}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">a.s.</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{n}=\hat{e}(Z_{n})\quad\text{a.s.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(Y;Z_{n})\;\geq\;I(Y;Z_{n-1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(Y;Z_{n})\;\geq\;I(Y;Z_{n-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(z):=R_{\hat{e}(z)}z." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(z):=R_{\hat{e}(z)}z.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{e}</annotation></semantics></math> is measurable and each <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\mapsto R_{e}z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\mapsto R_{e}z</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous, <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> is measurable.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N:=\{\omega\in\Omega:\ I_{n}(\omega)\neq\hat{e}(Z_{n}(\omega))\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N:=\{\omega\in\Omega:\ I_{n}(\omega)\neq\hat{e}(Z_{n}(\omega))\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">By identifiability, <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(N)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(N)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">For each <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\in\{1,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\in\{1,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math> let <math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{e}:=\mathsf{Supp}(X\mid I_{n}=e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖲𝗎𝗉𝗉</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{e}:=\mathsf{Supp}(X\mid I_{n}=e)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(X\in S_{e}\mid I_{n}=e)=1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(X\in S_{e}\mid I_{n}=e)=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(X\notin S_{e}\mid I_{n}=e)=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(X\notin S_{e}\mid I_{n}=e)=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M:=\{\omega\in\Omega:\ X(\omega)\notin S_{I_{n}(\omega)}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M:=\{\omega\in\Omega:\ X(\omega)\notin S_{I_{n}(\omega)}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(M)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{e=1}^{n}\mathbb{P}\big(M\cap\{I_{n}=e\}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{e=1}^{n}\mathbb{P}\big(M\cap\{I_{n}=e\}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{e=1}^{n}\mathbb{P}\big(\{X\notin S_{e}\}\cap\{I_{n}=e\}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{e=1}^{n}\mathbb{P}\big(\{X\notin S_{e}\}\cap\{I_{n}=e\}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{e=1}^{n}\mathbb{P}(I_{n}=e)\,\mathbb{P}(X\notin S_{e}\mid I_{n}=e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{e=1}^{n}\mathbb{P}(I_{n}=e)\,\mathbb{P}(X\notin S_{e}\mid I_{n}=e)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="A1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\in\Omega\setminus(N\cup M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\in\Omega\setminus(N\cup M)</annotation></semantics></math> and write</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x:=X(\omega),\quad e:=I_{n}(\omega),\quad z:=Z_{n}(\omega)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x:=X(\omega),\quad e:=I_{n}(\omega),\quad z:=Z_{n}(\omega).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=A^{(n)}_{e}x,\qquad e=\hat{e}(z),\qquad x\in S_{e}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=A^{(n)}_{e}x,\qquad e=\hat{e}(z),\qquad x\in S_{e}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the factorization-on-support assumption (applied to this <math id="A1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in S_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in S_{e}</annotation></semantics></math>),</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(n-1)}_{r_{n-1}(x)}x=R_{e}\,A^{(n)}_{e}x." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(n-1)}_{r_{n-1}(x)}x=R_{e}\,A^{(n)}_{e}x.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using <math id="A1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{n-1}(x)=r_{n-1}(X(\omega))=I_{n-1}(\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{n-1}(x)=r_{n-1}(X(\omega))=I_{n-1}(\omega)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(n)}_{e}x=z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(n)}_{e}x=z</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{n-1}(\omega)=A^{(n-1)}_{I_{n-1}(\omega)}X(\omega)=R_{e}\,z." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{n-1}(\omega)=A^{(n-1)}_{I_{n-1}(\omega)}X(\omega)=R_{e}\,z.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using <math id="A1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e=\hat{e}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e=\hat{e}(z)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{n-1}(\omega)=R_{\hat{e}(z)}z=h(z)=h(Z_{n}(\omega))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{n-1}(\omega)=R_{\hat{e}(z)}z=h(z)=h(Z_{n}(\omega)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{n-1}=h(Z_{n})\quad\text{a.s.}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>a.s.</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{n-1}=h(Z_{n})\quad\text{a.s.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U:=Z_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U:=Z_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V:=Z_{n-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V:=Z_{n-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=h(U)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=h(U)</annotation></semantics></math> almost surely. Hence</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(V)\subseteq\sigma(U)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(V)\subseteq\sigma(U).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(Y\mid U)\leq H(Y\mid V)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(Y\mid U)\leq H(Y\mid V).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">It follows that</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(Y;U)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(Y;U)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=H(Y)-H(Y\mid U)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=H(Y)-H(Y\mid U)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq H(Y)-H(Y\mid V)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq H(Y)-H(Y\mid V)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=I(Y;V)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=I(Y;V).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting <math id="A1.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=Z_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=Z_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=Z_{n-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=Z_{n-1}</annotation></semantics></math> yields</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(Y;Z_{n})\geq I(Y;Z_{n-1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(Y;Z_{n})\geq I(Y;Z_{n-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 1</span>
By induction, for any <math id="A1.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(Y;Z_{n})\geq I(Y;Z_{n-1})\geq\cdots\geq I(Y;Z_{1})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(Y;Z_{n})\geq I(Y;Z_{n-1})\geq\cdots\geq I(Y;Z_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p16.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, MoE with <math id="A1.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> experts preserves at least as much label information as a single-expert model.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.p17.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="101.84" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 101.84" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,101.84) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0.42 L 0 101.43 C 0 101.65 0.19 101.84 0.42 101.84 L 476.96 101.84 C 477.19 101.84 477.38 101.65 477.38 101.43 L 477.38 0.42 C 477.38 0.19 477.19 0 476.96 0 L 0.42 0 C 0.19 0 0 0.19 0 0.42 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#EDF8E8;" fill="#EDF8E8" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.42 0.42 L 0.42 101.43 L 476.96 101.43 L 476.96 0.42 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 5.95 89.32)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:6.18em;font-size:10pt;" height="94.09" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="503.26"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.p17.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.37em;">
<span id="A1.p17.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p17.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Practical Implication:<span id="A1.p17.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> While more experts can preserve more information, realizing this benefit requires sufficient training data per expert. Traditional MoE-PEFT suffers from data fragmentation as <math id="A1.p17.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> increases. LiME mitigates this via lightweight expert vectors and a shared PEFT backbone.<span id="A1.p17.pic1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3" title="3 LiME ‣ Lightweight Mixture of Experts for Efficient Multimodal Multi-task Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="85.79" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 85.79" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,85.79) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0.42 L 0 85.37 C 0 85.6 0.19 85.79 0.42 85.79 L 476.96 85.79 C 477.19 85.79 477.38 85.6 477.38 85.37 L 477.38 0.42 C 477.38 0.19 477.19 0 476.96 0 L 0.42 0 C 0.19 0 0 0.19 0 0.42 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#EDF8E8;" fill="#EDF8E8" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.42 0.42 L 0.42 85.37 L 476.96 85.37 L 476.96 0.42 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 5.95 73.41)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.62em;--ltx-fo-depth:5.03em;font-size:10pt;" height="78.04" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.51)" width="503.26"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.37em;">
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Overview:<span id="A2.p1.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> This theorem shows that LiME (shared PEFT with expert modulation) can approximate traditional MoE-PEFT (separate adapters per expert) with bounded performance gap. The key insight is that if the approximation error <math id="A2.p1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ε</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="1.110em">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> is small, the optimal risk differs by at most <math id="A2.p1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\bar{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ε</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="1.110em">¯</mo></mover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\bar{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="A2.p1.pic1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Smoothed quantitative equivalence: expert-specific PEFT vs. LiME)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Omega,\mathcal{F},\mathbb{P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Omega,\mathcal{F},\mathbb{P})</annotation></semantics></math> be a probability space.
Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X:\Omega\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X:\Omega\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y:\Omega\to\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y:\Omega\to\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> be random variables, where <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> is a standard Borel space.
Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0.1172,0.25,1}\mathbf{W}}_{0}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#1E40FF;" mathcolor="#1E40FF">𝐖</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0.1172,0.25,1}\mathbf{W}}_{0}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be fixed.
Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\{1,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\{1,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math> be measurable and define <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E:=r(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E:=r(X)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For each <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\in\{1,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\in\{1,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math> let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{\phi_{e}}}}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9C27FF;" mathcolor="#9C27FF">ϕ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9C27FF;" mathcolor="#9C27FF">𝐞</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{\phi_{e}}}}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be measurable and define the <span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">traditional MoE-PEFT</span> output (separate adapters per expert):</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{\text{MoE}}:={\color[rgb]{0.1172,0.25,1}\mathbf{W}}_{0}X+g_{{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{\phi_{E}}}}(X)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">MoE</mtext></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#1E40FF;" mathcolor="#1E40FF">𝐖</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9C27FF;" mathcolor="#9C27FF">ϕ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9C27FF;" mathcolor="#9C27FF">𝐄</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{\text{MoE}}:={\color[rgb]{0.1172,0.25,1}\mathbf{W}}_{0}X+g_{{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{\phi_{E}}}}(X)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{\phi}}}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9C27FF;" mathcolor="#9C27FF">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{\phi}}}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be measurable and for each <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math> let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{p}}_{e}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9C27FF;" mathcolor="#9C27FF">𝐩</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{p}}_{e}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define the <span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LiME</span> output (shared PEFT with expert modulation):</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{LiME}:={\color[rgb]{0.1172,0.25,1}\mathbf{W}}_{0}X+\big(g_{{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{\phi}}}(X)\odot{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{p}}_{E}\big)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#1E40FF;" mathcolor="#1E40FF">𝐖</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9C27FF;" mathcolor="#9C27FF">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9C27FF;" mathcolor="#9C27FF">𝐩</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{LiME}:={\color[rgb]{0.1172,0.25,1}\mathbf{W}}_{0}X+\big(g_{{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{\phi}}}(X)\odot{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{p}}_{E}\big)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume there exists <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\varepsilon}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\varepsilon}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big\|g_{{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{\phi_{E}}}}(X)-\big(g_{{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{\phi}}}(X)\odot{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{p}}_{E}\big)\big\|_{2}\leq\overline{\varepsilon}\quad\text{a.s.}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9C27FF;" mathcolor="#9C27FF">ϕ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9C27FF;" mathcolor="#9C27FF">𝐄</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9C27FF;" mathcolor="#9C27FF">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9C27FF;" mathcolor="#9C27FF">𝐩</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">a.s.</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big\|g_{{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{\phi_{E}}}}(X)-\big(g_{{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{\phi}}}(X)\odot{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{p}}_{E}\big)\big\|_{2}\leq\overline{\varepsilon}\quad\text{a.s.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2}I_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2}I_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> be independent of <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,E,Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,E,Y)</annotation></semantics></math> and define</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{(\sigma)}_{\text{MoE}}:=Z_{\text{MoE}}+N,\qquad U^{(\sigma)}_{LiME}:=Z_{LiME}+N." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">MoE</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">MoE</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{(\sigma)}_{\text{MoE}}:=Z_{\text{MoE}}+N,\qquad U^{(\sigma)}_{LiME}:=Z_{LiME}+N.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> be a standard Borel space and let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell:\mathcal{Y}\times\mathcal{A}\to[0,L_{\max}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell:\mathcal{Y}\times\mathcal{A}\to[0,L_{\max}]</annotation></semantics></math> be measurable.
For a random element <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> taking values in <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> define</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}^{*}(U):=\inf_{\delta}\mathbb{E}\big[\ell\big(Y,\delta(U)\big)\big]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mi>δ</mi></munder><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}^{*}(U):=\inf_{\delta}\mathbb{E}\big[\ell\big(Y,\delta(U)\big)\big],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the infimum is over all measurable <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big|\mathcal{R}^{*}(U^{(\sigma)}_{\text{MoE}})-\mathcal{R}^{*}(U^{(\sigma)}_{LiME})\big|\leq L_{\max}\cdot\frac{\overline{\varepsilon}}{2\sigma}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">MoE</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big|\mathcal{R}^{*}(U^{(\sigma)}_{\text{MoE}})-\mathcal{R}^{*}(U^{(\sigma)}_{LiME})\big|\leq L_{\max}\cdot\frac{\overline{\varepsilon}}{2\sigma}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define measurable maps <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\text{MoE}},m_{LiME}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\{1,\dots,n\}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext>MoE</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\text{MoE}},m_{LiME}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\{1,\dots,n\}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\text{MoE}}(x,e):={\color[rgb]{0.1172,0.25,1}\mathbf{W}}_{0}x+g_{{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{\phi_{e}}}}(x)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext>MoE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#1E40FF;" mathcolor="#1E40FF">𝐖</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9C27FF;" mathcolor="#9C27FF">ϕ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9C27FF;" mathcolor="#9C27FF">𝐞</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\text{MoE}}(x,e):={\color[rgb]{0.1172,0.25,1}\mathbf{W}}_{0}x+g_{{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{\phi_{e}}}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{LiME}(x,e):={\color[rgb]{0.1172,0.25,1}\mathbf{W}}_{0}x+\big(g_{{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{\phi}}}(x)\odot{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{p}}_{e}\big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#1E40FF;" mathcolor="#1E40FF">𝐖</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9C27FF;" mathcolor="#9C27FF">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9C27FF;" mathcolor="#9C27FF">𝐩</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{LiME}(x,e):={\color[rgb]{0.1172,0.25,1}\mathbf{W}}_{0}x+\big(g_{{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{\phi}}}(x)\odot{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{p}}_{e}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{\text{MoE}}=m_{\text{MoE}}(X,E),\qquad Z_{LiME}=m_{LiME}(X,E)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mtext>MoE</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext>MoE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{\text{MoE}}=m_{\text{MoE}}(X,E),\qquad Z_{LiME}=m_{LiME}(X,E),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{(\sigma)}_{\text{MoE}}=m_{\text{MoE}}(X,E)+N" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mtext>MoE</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext>MoE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{(\sigma)}_{\text{MoE}}=m_{\text{MoE}}(X,E)+N</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{(\sigma)}_{LiME}=m_{LiME}(X,E)+N" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{(\sigma)}_{LiME}=m_{LiME}(X,E)+N</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma:=\sigma^{2}I_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma:=\sigma^{2}I_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,E,Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,E,Y)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}\big(U^{(\sigma)}_{\text{MoE}}\mid X,E\big)=\mathcal{N}\big(m_{\text{MoE}}(X,E),\Sigma\big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mtext>MoE</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext>MoE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}\big(U^{(\sigma)}_{\text{MoE}}\mid X,E\big)=\mathcal{N}\big(m_{\text{MoE}}(X,E),\Sigma\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}\big(U^{(\sigma)}_{LiME}\mid X,E\big)=\mathcal{N}\big(m_{LiME}(X,E),\Sigma\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}\big(U^{(\sigma)}_{LiME}\mid X,E\big)=\mathcal{N}\big(m_{LiME}(X,E),\Sigma\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">For any <math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{1},\mu_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{1},\mu_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{KL}\!\left(\mathcal{N}(\mu_{1},\Sigma)\,\middle\|\,\mathcal{N}(\mu_{2},\Sigma)\right)=\frac{\|\mu_{1}-\mu_{2}\|_{2}^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.431em;" width="1.431em"><mi>KL</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">∥</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}\!\left(\mathcal{N}(\mu_{1},\Sigma)\,\middle\|\,\mathcal{N}(\mu_{2},\Sigma)\right)=\frac{\|\mu_{1}-\mu_{2}\|_{2}^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{KL}\!\left(\mathcal{L}\big(U^{(\sigma)}_{\text{MoE}}\mid X,E\big)\,\middle\|\,\mathcal{L}\big(U^{(\sigma)}_{LiME}\mid X,E\big)\right)=" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.431em;" width="1.431em"><mi>KL</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mtext>MoE</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">∥</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}\!\left(\mathcal{L}\big(U^{(\sigma)}_{\text{MoE}}\mid X,E\big)\,\middle\|\,\mathcal{L}\big(U^{(\sigma)}_{LiME}\mid X,E\big)\right)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\|m_{\text{MoE}}(X,E)-m_{LiME}(X,E)\|_{2}^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext>MoE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\|m_{\text{MoE}}(X,E)-m_{LiME}(X,E)\|_{2}^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">By Pinsker’s inequality,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}(P,Q)\leq\sqrt{\tfrac{1}{2}\,\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}(P,Q)\leq\sqrt{\tfrac{1}{2}\,\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.8.1" class="ltx_text">Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}\!\left(\mathcal{L}\big(U^{(\sigma)}_{\text{MoE}}\mid X,E\big),\mathcal{L}\big(U^{(\sigma)}_{LiME}\mid X,E\big)\right)\leq" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.359em;" width="1.359em"><mi>TV</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mtext>MoE</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}\!\left(\mathcal{L}\big(U^{(\sigma)}_{\text{MoE}}\mid X,E\big),\mathcal{L}\big(U^{(\sigma)}_{LiME}\mid X,E\big)\right)\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hfill\frac{\|m_{\text{MoE}}(X,E)-m_{LiME}(X,E)\|_{2}}{2\sigma}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext>MoE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hfill\frac{\|m_{\text{MoE}}(X,E)-m_{LiME}(X,E)\|_{2}}{2\sigma}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.9.1" class="ltx_text">Since</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\text{MoE}}(X,E)-m_{LiME}(X,E)=" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext>MoE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\text{MoE}}(X,E)-m_{LiME}(X,E)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{\phi_{E}}}}(X)-\big(g_{{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{\phi}}}(X)\odot{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{p}}_{E}\big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9C27FF;" mathcolor="#9C27FF">ϕ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9C27FF;" mathcolor="#9C27FF">𝐄</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9C27FF;" mathcolor="#9C27FF">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9C27FF;" mathcolor="#9C27FF">𝐩</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{\phi_{E}}}}(X)-\big(g_{{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{\phi}}}(X)\odot{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{p}}_{E}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.10.1" class="ltx_text">the assumption implies</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}\!\left(\mathcal{L}\big(U^{(\sigma)}_{\text{MoE}}\mid X,E\big),\mathcal{L}\big(U^{(\sigma)}_{LiME}\mid X,E\big)\right)\leq\frac{\overline{\varepsilon}}{2\sigma}\hskip 9.24994pt\text{a.s.}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.379em;" width="1.379em"><mi mathsize="0.900em">TV</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">U</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">MoE</mtext><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">σ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">E</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">U</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">E</mi></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">σ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">E</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">ε</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">σ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.930em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext mathsize="0.900em">a.s.</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}\!\left(\mathcal{L}\big(U^{(\sigma)}_{\text{MoE}}\mid X,E\big),\mathcal{L}\big(U^{(\sigma)}_{LiME}\mid X,E\big)\right)\leq\frac{\overline{\varepsilon}}{2\sigma}\hskip 9.24994pt\text{a.s.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.11.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\text{MoE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mtext>MoE</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\text{MoE}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{LiME}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{LiME}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the joint laws of
<math id="A2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Y,U^{(\sigma)}_{\text{MoE}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mtext>MoE</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Y,U^{(\sigma)}_{\text{MoE}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Y,U^{(\sigma)}_{LiME})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Y,U^{(\sigma)}_{LiME})</annotation></semantics></math>.
For any measurable <math id="A2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\subseteq\mathcal{Y}\times\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\subseteq\mathcal{Y}\times\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\big|P^{\text{MoE}}(B)-P^{LiME}(B)\big|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mtext>MoE</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\big|P^{\text{MoE}}(B)-P^{LiME}(B)\big|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\left|\mathbb{E}\!\left[\mathbb{P}\big((Y,U^{(\sigma)}_{\text{MoE}})\in B\mid X,E,Y\big)\right.\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mtext>MoE</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left|\mathbb{E}\!\left[\mathbb{P}\big((Y,U^{(\sigma)}_{\text{MoE}})\in B\mid X,E,Y\big)\right.\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\left.\left.-\mathbb{P}\big((Y,U^{(\sigma)}_{LiME})\in B\mid X,E,Y\big)\right]\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo><mo fence="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\left.\left.-\mathbb{P}\big((Y,U^{(\sigma)}_{LiME})\in B\mid X,E,Y\big)\right]\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}\!\left[\mathrm{TV}\!\left(\mathcal{L}\big(U^{(\sigma)}_{\text{MoE}}\mid X,E\big),\right.\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><mpadded style="width:1.359em;" width="1.359em"><mi>TV</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mtext>MoE</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}\!\left[\mathrm{TV}\!\left(\mathcal{L}\big(U^{(\sigma)}_{\text{MoE}}\mid X,E\big),\right.\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\left.\left.\mathcal{L}\big(U^{(\sigma)}_{LiME}\mid X,E\big)\right)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\left.\left.\mathcal{L}\big(U^{(\sigma)}_{LiME}\mid X,E\big)\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.12.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the supremum over <math id="A2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}\big(P^{\text{MoE}},P^{LiME}\big)\leq" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">P</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">MoE</mtext></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">P</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">E</mi></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}\big(P^{\text{MoE}},P^{LiME}\big)\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\mathrm{TV}\!\left(\mathcal{L}\big(U^{(\sigma)}_{\text{MoE}}\mid X,E\big),\mathcal{L}\big(U^{(\sigma)}_{LiME}\mid X,E\big)\right)\right]\leq\frac{\overline{\varepsilon}}{2\sigma}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.517em;" width="0.517em"><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.379em;" width="1.379em"><mi mathsize="0.900em">TV</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">U</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">MoE</mtext><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">σ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">E</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">U</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">E</mi></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">σ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">E</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">ε</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">σ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\mathrm{TV}\!\left(\mathcal{L}\big(U^{(\sigma)}_{\text{MoE}}\mid X,E\big),\mathcal{L}\big(U^{(\sigma)}_{LiME}\mid X,E\big)\right)\right]\leq\frac{\overline{\varepsilon}}{2\sigma}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix any measurable <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and define</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\text{MoE}}(\delta):=\mathbb{E}\big[\ell\big(Y,\delta(U^{(\sigma)}_{\text{MoE}})\big)\big]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mtext>MoE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mtext>MoE</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\text{MoE}}(\delta):=\mathbb{E}\big[\ell\big(Y,\delta(U^{(\sigma)}_{\text{MoE}})\big)\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{LiME}(\delta):=\mathbb{E}\big[\ell\big(Y,\delta(U^{(\sigma)}_{LiME})\big)\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{LiME}(\delta):=\mathbb{E}\big[\ell\big(Y,\delta(U^{(\sigma)}_{LiME})\big)\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Define</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(y,u):=\frac{\ell\big(y,\delta(u)\big)}{L_{\max}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(y,u):=\frac{\ell\big(y,\delta(u)\big)}{L_{\max}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">so that <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq f\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq f\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
