<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="85.1" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 85.1" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,85.1) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0.42 L 0 84.68 C 0 84.91 0.19 85.1 0.42 85.1 L 476.96 85.1 C 477.19 85.1 477.38 84.91 477.38 84.68 L 477.38 0.42 C 477.38 0.19 477.19 0 476.96 0 L 0.42 0 C 0.19 0 0 0.19 0 0.42 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#EDF8E8;" fill="#EDF8E8" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.42 0.42 L 0.42 84.68 L 476.96 84.68 L 476.96 0.42 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 5.95 72.71)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.62em;--ltx-fo-depth:4.98em;font-size:10pt;" height="77.35" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.51)" width="503.26"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.37em;">
<span id="A2.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Interpretation:<span id="A2.p4.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The bound <math id="A2.p4.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\max}\cdot\frac{\bar{\varepsilon}}{2\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">L</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">max</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ε</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="1.580em">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">σ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\max}\cdot\frac{\bar{\varepsilon}}{2\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> shows that if the modulation <math id="A2.p4.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{\phi}}}(x)\odot{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{p}}_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">g</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9C27FF;" mathcolor="#9C27FF" mathvariant="normal">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9C27FF;" mathcolor="#9C27FF">𝐩</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">e</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{\phi}}}(x)\odot{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{p}}_{e}</annotation></semantics></math> closely approximates the expert-specific adapter <math id="A2.p4.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{\phi_{e}}}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">g</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9C27FF;" mathcolor="#9C27FF" mathvariant="normal">ϕ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9C27FF;" mathcolor="#9C27FF">𝐞</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{{\color[rgb]{0.6133,0.1523,1}\mathbf{\phi_{e}}}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, then LiME achieves nearly the same optimal risk as traditional MoE-PEFT. Our empirical results (CKA <math id="A2.p4.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≈</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx</annotation></semantics></math> 0.935) confirm this approximation is tight in practice.<span id="A2.p4.pic1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A2.T3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="A2.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">CKA (Centered Kernel Alignment) similarity scores between LiMELoRA and MoELoRA across layers and GLUE datasets. Higher values indicate stronger representational similarity.</span></figcaption>
