<td id="A2.T3.5.1.25.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A2.T3.5.1.25.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.954</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.5.1.25.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A2.T3.5.1.25.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.945</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.5.1.25.8" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A2.T3.5.1.25.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">0.960</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T3.5.1.26" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E8F5E0;">
<td id="A2.T3.5.1.26.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bbbb ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A2.T3.5.1.26.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-bg-color:#E8F5E0;">Mean</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.5.1.26.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bbbb ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A2.T3.5.1.26.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-bg-color:#E8F5E0;">0.942</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.5.1.26.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bbbb ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A2.T3.5.1.26.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-bg-color:#E8F5E0;">0.939</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.5.1.26.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bbbb ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A2.T3.5.1.26.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-bg-color:#E8F5E0;">0.931</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.5.1.26.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bbbb ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A2.T3.5.1.26.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-bg-color:#E8F5E0;">0.939</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.5.1.26.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bbbb ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A2.T3.5.1.26.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-bg-color:#E8F5E0;">0.931</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.5.1.26.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bbbb ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A2.T3.5.1.26.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-bg-color:#E8F5E0;">0.929</span></td>
<td id="A2.T3.5.1.26.8" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bbbb ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.25pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A2.T3.5.1.26.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-bg-color:#E8F5E0;">0.935</span></td></tr>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>CKA Analysis</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To provide empirical validation of Theorem <a href="#S3" title="3 LiME ‣ Lightweight Mixture of Experts for Efficient Multimodal Multi-task Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we analyze CKA (Centered Kernel Alignment) similarity between LiMELoRA and MoELoRA representations at each layer. CKA measures representational similarity independent of orthogonal transformations and isotropic scaling, making it suitable for comparing learned representations across architectures. Table <a href="#A2.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem ‣ Lightweight Mixture of Experts for Efficient Multimodal Multi-task Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> shows CKA scores for layers 0–23 across all GLUE tasks.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Several observations emerge. First, CKA remains consistently high (<math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;0.88" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.88</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;0.88</annotation></semantics></math>) across all layers, indicating that LiME approximates full MoE-PEFT throughout the network, not just at specific layers. Second, early layers (0–3) show the highest CKA (0.949–0.994), suggesting that expert modulation most closely matches separate adapters when processing lower-level features. Third, certain middle layers (9, 17, 19) show relatively lower CKA (0.880–0.897), which may reflect increased task-specific specialization where the modulation approximation is less tight. Fourth, the final layer (23) recovers high CKA (0.960), indicating that output representations converge despite intermediate differences—consistent with our theoretical bound that approximation error remains controlled. The overall mean CKA of 0.935 across all layers and tasks confirms that LiME effectively approximates expert-specific PEFT, empirically supporting Theorem <a href="#S3" title="3 LiME ‣ Lightweight Mixture of Experts for Efficient Multimodal Multi-task Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3" title="3 LiME ‣ Lightweight Mixture of Experts for Efficient Multimodal Multi-task Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="68.49" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 68.49" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,68.49) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0.42 L 0 68.08 C 0 68.31 0.19 68.49 0.42 68.49 L 476.96 68.49 C 477.19 68.49 477.38 68.31 477.38 68.08 L 477.38 0.42 C 477.38 0.19 477.19 0 476.96 0 L 0.42 0 C 0.19 0 0 0.19 0 0.42 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#EDF8E8;" fill="#EDF8E8" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.42 0.42 L 0.42 68.08 L 476.96 68.08 L 476.96 0.42 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 5.95 56.11)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.62em;--ltx-fo-depth:3.78em;font-size:10pt;" height="60.75" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.51)" width="503.26"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.37em;">
<span id="A3.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Intuition:<span id="A3.p1.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> In causal (autoregressive) models, each position can only attend to previous positions. Therefore, later hidden states within an n-gram window accumulate more context, and adding more context cannot reduce information about the target <math id="A3.p1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="A3.p1.pic1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We first establish the necessary definitions, then prove the main result.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Mutual Information)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For random variables <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(A;B)=H(B)-H(B\mid A)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(A;B)=H(B)-H(B\mid A)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition C.2</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Conditional Mutual Information)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For random variables <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(A;B\mid C)=H(B\mid C)-H(B\mid A,C)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(A;B\mid C)=H(B\mid C)-H(B\mid A,C)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem C.3</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Routing Informativeness in Causal N-gram Windows)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{1},h_{2},\ldots,h_{n}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{1},h_{2},\ldots,h_{n}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be hidden states within an n-gram window under causal attention, and let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> denote the task objective. Then the routing informativeness is maximized at the window’s final position:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(Y;h_{n})\geq I(Y;h_{n-1})\geq\cdots\geq I(Y;h_{1})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(Y;h_{n})\geq I(Y;h_{n-1})\geq\cdots\geq I(Y;h_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Under causal attention, hidden state <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> aggregates information from all preceding positions. Define the cumulative context <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h_{1:t}=(h_{1},h_{2},\ldots,h_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{1:t}=(h_{1},h_{2},\ldots,h_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. By the data processing inequality, since <math id="A3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is a deterministic function of <math id="A3.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h_{1:t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{1:t}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="I(Y;h_{t})\leq I(Y;h_{1:t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(Y;h_{t})\leq I(Y;h_{1:t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">It suffices to show that <math id="A3.p4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="I(Y;h_{1:t+1})\geq I(Y;h_{1:t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(Y;h_{1:t+1})\geq I(Y;h_{1:t})</annotation></semantics></math> for an arbitrary index <math id="A3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{1,2,\ldots,n-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{1,2,\ldots,n-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the chain rule for mutual information:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="I(Y;h_{1:t+1})=I(Y;h_{1:t})+I(Y;h_{t+1}\mid h_{1:t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(Y;h_{1:t+1})=I(Y;h_{1:t})+I(Y;h_{t+1}\mid h_{1:t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">To verify this, we expand the right-hand side using Definitions 1 and 2:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle I(Y;h_{1:t})+I(Y;h_{t+1}\mid h_{1:t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(Y;h_{1:t})+I(Y;h_{t+1}\mid h_{1:t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\big[H(Y)-H(Y\mid h_{1:t})\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\big[H(Y)-H(Y\mid h_{1:t})\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\big[H(Y\mid h_{1:t})-H(Y\mid h_{1:t},h_{t+1})\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\big[H(Y\mid h_{1:t})-H(Y\mid h_{1:t},h_{t+1})\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=H(Y)-H(Y\mid h_{1:t},h_{t+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=H(Y)-H(Y\mid h_{1:t},h_{t+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=I(Y;h_{1:t+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=I(Y;h_{1:t+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since conditional mutual information is non-negative <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cover, 1999</a>)</cite>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="I(Y;h_{t+1}\mid h_{1:t})\geq 0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(Y;h_{t+1}\mid h_{1:t})\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">it follows immediately that:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="I(Y;h_{1:t+1})\geq I(Y;h_{1:t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(Y;h_{1:t+1})\geq I(Y;h_{1:t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since causal attention ensures <math id="A3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> encodes <math id="A3.p9.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h_{1:t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{1:t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A3.p9.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="I(Y;h_{t})=I(Y;h_{1:t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(Y;h_{t})=I(Y;h_{1:t})</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying this equality and the above inequality iteratively for <math id="A3.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=n-1,n-2,\ldots,1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=n-1,n-2,\ldots,1</annotation></semantics></math> completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.p10.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="85.24" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 85.24" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,85.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0.42 L 0 84.82 C 0 85.05 0.19 85.24 0.42 85.24 L 476.96 85.24 C 477.19 85.24 477.38 85.05 477.38 84.82 L 477.38 0.42 C 477.38 0.19 477.19 0 476.96 0 L 0.42 0 C 0.19 0 0 0.19 0 0.42 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#EDF8E8;" fill="#EDF8E8" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.42 0.42 L 0.42 84.82 L 476.96 84.82 L 476.96 0.42 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 5.95 72.71)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:4.98em;font-size:10pt;" height="77.49" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="503.26"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.p10.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.37em;">
<span id="A3.p10.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p10.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Implication for Routing:<span id="A3.p10.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> In causal models, the last hidden state <math id="A3.p10.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">h</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> of each n-gram window has access to all preceding positions via causal attention, capturing the most task-relevant information. This justifies LiME’s last-token routing strategy for n-gram windowed routing.<span id="A3.p10.pic1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Expert Selection Strategies</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(x)=[w_{1}(x),w_{2}(x),\ldots,w_{E}(x)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(x)=[w_{1}(x),w_{2}(x),\ldots,w_{E}(x)]</annotation></semantics></math> denote the routing probability distribution over <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> experts for input <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, obtained via softmax over routing scores:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}(x)=\frac{\exp(s_{i}(x))}{\sum_{j=1}^{E}\exp(s_{j}(x))}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}(x)=\frac{\exp(s_{i}(x))}{\sum_{j=1}^{E}\exp(s_{j}(x))}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We define <math id="A4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{[i]}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{[i]}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> as the <math id="A4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th largest probability, i.e., <math id="A4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{[1]}(x)\geq w_{[2]}(x)\geq\cdots\geq w_{[E]}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{[1]}(x)\geq w_{[2]}(x)\geq\cdots\geq w_{[E]}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. Each selection strategy defines a set of activated experts <math id="A4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}(x)\subseteq\{1,\ldots,E\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}(x)\subseteq\{1,\ldots,E\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Given a selected set <math id="A4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, the renormalized weights are computed as:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{w}_{i}(x)=\begin{cases}\displaystyle\frac{w_{i}(x)}{\sum_{j\in\mathcal{S}(x)}w_{j}(x)}&amp;\text{if }i\in\mathcal{S}(x)\\[8.61108pt]
0&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{w}_{i}(x)=\begin{cases}\displaystyle\frac{w_{i}(x)}{\sum_{j\in\mathcal{S}(x)}w_{j}(x)}&amp;\text{if }i\in\mathcal{S}(x)\\[8.61108pt]
0&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Each strategy below differs only in how <math id="A4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is defined.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Fixed Top-K</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The most common approach selects a fixed number of <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> experts with highest routing probabilities, regardless of the distribution shape.</p>
<table id="A4.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{k}(x)=\left\{i:w_{i}(x)\geq w_{[k]}(x)\right\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{k}(x)=\left\{i:w_{i}(x)\geq w_{[k]}(x)\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Properties:</span> Constant computational cost with exactly <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> experts activated. However, it ignores the confidence signal—a dominant expert at 90% is treated the same as a marginal leader at 15%.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Absolute Threshold</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This strategy selects all experts whose probability exceeds a fixed threshold <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A4.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{\eta}(x)=\left\{i:w_{i}(x)\geq\eta\right\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{\eta}(x)=\left\{i:w_{i}(x)\geq\eta\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">To ensure at least one expert is selected, we enforce:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{\eta}(x)=\begin{cases}\left\{i:w_{i}(x)\geq\eta\right\}&amp;\text{if }\exists\,i:w_{i}(x)\geq\eta\\[4.30554pt]
\left\{\arg\max_{i}w_{i}(x)\right\}&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∃</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{\eta}(x)=\begin{cases}\left\{i:w_{i}(x)\geq\eta\right\}&amp;\text{if }\exists\,i:w_{i}(x)\geq\eta\\[4.30554pt]
\left\{\arg\max_{i}w_{i}(x)\right\}&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Properties:</span> Adaptive to routing confidence. However, not scale-invariant with respect to <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>. For uniform distribution, <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}=1/E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}=1/E</annotation></semantics></math>, so the threshold <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> must satisfy <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&lt;1/E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&lt;1/E</annotation></semantics></math> to select any expert. This makes <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> difficult to tune across different expert counts.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Entropy-Based Selection</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This strategy uses the entropy of the routing distribution to determine the number of activated experts. High entropy indicates uncertainty (select more experts); low entropy indicates confidence (select fewer).</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The entropy of the routing distribution is:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H(x)=-\sum_{i=1}^{E}w_{i}(x)\log w_{i}(x)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>E</mi></munderover><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(x)=-\sum_{i=1}^{E}w_{i}(x)\log w_{i}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Normalized by maximum entropy <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\max}=\log E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\max}=\log E</annotation></semantics></math> (achieved by uniform distribution):</p>
<table id="A4.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{H}(x)=\frac{H(x)}{\log E}\in[0,1]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{H}(x)=\frac{H(x)}{\log E}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">The number of experts is determined by linear interpolation:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k(x)=k_{\min}+\left\lfloor(k_{\max}-k_{\min})\cdot\bar{H}(x)\right\rfloor" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⌋</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k(x)=k_{\min}+\left\lfloor(k_{\max}-k_{\min})\cdot\bar{H}(x)\right\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p">The selected set is then:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{H}(x)=\left\{i:w_{i}(x)\geq w_{[k(x)]}(x)\right\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{H}(x)=\left\{i:w_{i}(x)\geq w_{[k(x)]}(x)\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Properties:</span> Theoretically motivated and scale-invariant. However, requires tuning two hyperparameters (<math id="A4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\min},k_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\min},k_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>), and the linear mapping may not be optimal.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Gini-Based Selection</h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Gini coefficient measures inequality in the distribution. High Gini indicates dominance by few experts; low Gini indicates uniform spread.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The Gini coefficient for routing probabilities (noting <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}w_{i}(x)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}w_{i}(x)=1</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<table id="A4.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(x)=\frac{1}{2E}\sum_{i=1}^{E}\sum_{j=1}^{E}|w_{i}(x)-w_{j}(x)|\in\left[0,1-\frac{1}{E}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>E</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>E</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>E</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(x)=\frac{1}{2E}\sum_{i=1}^{E}\sum_{j=1}^{E}|w_{i}(x)-w_{j}(x)|\in\left[0,1-\frac{1}{E}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">An equivalent formulation using sorted probabilities:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(x)=\frac{2\sum_{i=1}^{E}i\cdot w_{[E-i+1]}(x)}{E}-\frac{E+1}{E}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>E</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>E</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(x)=\frac{2\sum_{i=1}^{E}i\cdot w_{[E-i+1]}(x)}{E}-\frac{E+1}{E}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p">The number of experts (inverse relationship—high Gini means fewer experts):</p>
<table id="A4.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k(x)=k_{\max}-\left\lfloor(k_{\max}-k_{\min})\cdot\frac{G(x)}{1-1/E}\right\rfloor" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>⌋</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k(x)=k_{\max}-\left\lfloor(k_{\max}-k_{\min})\cdot\frac{G(x)}{1-1/E}\right\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.4" class="ltx_p">The selected set is then:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{G}(x)=\left\{i:w_{i}(x)\geq w_{[k(x)]}(x)\right\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{G}(x)=\left\{i:w_{i}(x)\geq w_{[k(x)]}(x)\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Properties:</span> More sensitive to distribution tails than entropy. However, <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(E^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(E^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> computation for the double sum (or <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(E\log E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(E\log E)</annotation></semantics></math> with sorting), and requires two hyperparameters.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.5 </span>Cumulative Probability Selection</h3>

<div id="A4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This strategy selects the minimum number of experts whose cumulative probability reaches a target threshold <math id="A4.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A4.Ex82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k(x)=\min\left\{k:\sum_{i=1}^{k}w_{[i]}(x)\geq\rho\right\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.111em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k(x)=\min\left\{k:\sum_{i=1}^{k}w_{[i]}(x)\geq\rho\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The selected set contains the top-<math id="A4.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k(x)</annotation></semantics></math> experts:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{\rho}(x)=\left\{i:w_{i}(x)\geq w_{[k(x)]}(x)\right\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{\rho}(x)=\left\{i:w_{i}(x)\geq w_{[k(x)]}(x)\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Properties:</span> Intuitive interpretation—with <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>, selected experts capture 90% of the routing signal. Scale-invariant and single hyperparameter. However, requires sorting (<math id="A4.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(E\log E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(E\log E)</annotation></semantics></math>) and may over-select on flat distributions (e.g., uniform distribution with <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=4</annotation></semantics></math> requires all 4 experts to reach <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.6 </span>Top-K with Minimum Gap</h3>

<div id="A4.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This strategy extends fixed top-<math id="A4.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> by including additional experts that are within a margin <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> of the <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th expert.</p>
<table id="A4.Ex84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{k,\Delta}(x)=\left\{i:w_{i}(x)\geq w_{[k]}(x)-\Delta\right\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{k,\Delta}(x)=\left\{i:w_{i}(x)\geq w_{[k]}(x)-\Delta\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Equivalently:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{k,\Delta}(x)=\mathcal{S}_{k}(x)\cup\left\{i\,\middle|\,w_{[k]}(x)-\Delta\leq w_{i}(x)&lt;w_{[k]}(x)\right\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{k,\Delta}(x)=\mathcal{S}_{k}(x)\cup\left\{i\,\middle|\,w_{[k]}(x)-\Delta\leq w_{i}(x)&lt;w_{[k]}(x)\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Properties:</span> Addresses arbitrary cutoffs when experts have similar scores. However, requires tuning two hyperparameters (<math id="A4.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k,\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k,\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>), and <math id="A4.SS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> is not scale-invariant.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.7 </span>Relative Threshold (Ours)</h3>

<div id="A4.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We select all experts whose probability is at least a fraction <math id="A4.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> of the maximum probability.</p>
<table id="A4.Ex86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{\theta}(x)=\left\{i:w_{i}(x)\geq\theta\cdot w_{[1]}(x)\right\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{\theta}(x)=\left\{i:w_{i}(x)\geq\theta\cdot w_{[1]}(x)\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS7.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{[1]}(x)=\max_{j}w_{j}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{[1]}(x)=\max_{j}w_{j}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS7.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS7.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Analysis of selected expert count.</span> Let <math id="A4.SS7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}(x)=w_{i}(x)/w_{[1]}(x)\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}(x)=w_{i}(x)/w_{[1]}(x)\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> be the relative probability of expert <math id="A4.SS7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Then:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{S}_{\theta}(x)|=\left|\left\{i:r_{i}(x)\geq\theta\right\}\right|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{S}_{\theta}(x)|=\left|\left\{i:r_{i}(x)\geq\theta\right\}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS7.p2.2" class="ltx_p">For a peaked distribution where <math id="A4.SS7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{[1]}(x)\gg w_{[2]}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{[1]}(x)\gg w_{[2]}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A4.SS7.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{[2]}(x)\ll 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≪</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{[2]}(x)\ll 1</annotation></semantics></math>, so only the top expert is selected when <math id="A4.SS7.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta&gt;r_{[2]}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta&gt;r_{[2]}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. For a flat distribution where <math id="A4.SS7.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{[1]}(x)\approx w_{[2]}(x)\approx\cdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≈</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{[1]}(x)\approx w_{[2]}(x)\approx\cdots</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A4.SS7.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}(x)\approx 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}(x)\approx 1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.SS7.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, so most experts are selected.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS7.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A4.SS7.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="69.32" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 69.32" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,69.32) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0.42 L 0 68.91 C 0 69.14 0.19 69.32 0.42 69.32 L 476.96 69.32 C 477.19 69.32 477.38 69.14 477.38 68.91 L 477.38 0.42 C 477.38 0.19 477.19 0 476.96 0 L 0.42 0 C 0.19 0 0 0.19 0 0.42 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#EDF8E8;" fill="#EDF8E8" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.42 0.42 L 0.42 68.91 L 476.96 68.91 L 476.96 0.42 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 5.95 56.8)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:3.83em;font-size:10pt;" height="61.58" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="503.26"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A4.SS7.p3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.37em;">
<span id="A4.SS7.p3.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS7.p3.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Why Relative Threshold:<span id="A4.SS7.p3.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> (i) Scale-invariant across different <math id="A4.SS7.p3.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>. (ii) Single hyperparameter <math id="A4.SS7.p3.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>. (iii) <math id="A4.SS7.p3.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">E</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(E)</annotation></semantics></math> computation. (iv) Interpretable: <math id="A4.SS7.p3.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> means “at least half as good as the best.” (v) Guarantees at least one expert selected.<span id="A4.SS7.p3.pic1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A4.T4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="A4.T4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Comparison of expert selection strategies.</span></figcaption>
<table id="A4.T4.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A4.T4.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tttt"><span id="A4.T4.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Strategy</span></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tttt"><span id="A4.T4.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Selection Rule</span></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tttt"><span id="A4.T4.5.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Hyperparams</span></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tttt"><span id="A4.T4.5.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Complexity</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="A4.T4.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Fixed Top-K</span></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A4.T4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}(x)\geq w_{[k]}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}(x)\geq w_{[k]}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A4.T4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A4.T4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">E</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(E)</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.5.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A4.T4.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Absolute Threshold</span></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.T4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}(x)\geq\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≥</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}(x)\geq\eta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.T4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.T4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">E</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(E)</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.5.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A4.T4.5.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Entropy-Based</span></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.T4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}(x)\geq w_{[k(H)]}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">H</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}(x)\geq w_{[k(H)]}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.T4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\min},k_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">min</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\min},k_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.T4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">E</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(E)</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.5.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A4.T4.5.5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Gini-Based</span></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.T4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}(x)\geq w_{[k(G)]}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">G</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}(x)\geq w_{[k(G)]}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.T4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\min},k_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">min</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\min},k_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.T4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(E^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">E</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(E^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.5.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A4.T4.5.6.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Cumulative Prob.</span></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.T4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j\leq i}w_{[j]}(x)\geq\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≥</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j\leq i}w_{[j]}(x)\geq\rho</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.T4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.T4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(E\log E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">E</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">E</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(E\log E)</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
